# Git Commit Messages

When creating or amending commits in this project:

1. Always write commit messages in **English**.
2. Use this shape (title + blank line + dash bullets), matching recent mainline style (e.g. `80b90c1`):

```text
type(scope): short imperative summary

- First concrete change in one sentence.

- Second concrete change in one sentence.
```

## Rules

- Title: conventional commits (`fix` / `feat` / `refactor` / `docs` / `test` / `chore`, …) with an optional scope.
- Keep the summary short and imperative; focus on **why**/effect, not a file list.
- Body: one or more `- ` bullets; each bullet is a full sentence ending with a period.
- Prefer a blank line between bullets when matching the reference style above.
- Do not write commit titles or bodies in Chinese.
